        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: वापी",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वापी — vāpī — \"an oblong reservoir; a tank\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ग्रामस्य मध्ये गभीरा वापी अस्ति। grāmasya madhye gabhīrā vāpī asti. In the middle of the village there is a deep reservoir."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वापी (vāpī) comes from the root √vap, \"to strew, to heap up\", which also gives vapati, \"sows\": MW gives vāpī as a pond made by damming up earth, an oblong reservoir, a tank; it lives on as Hindi bāuṛī, \"a well with steps\" (MW; CDIAL 11529)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
